# @agent-k/chat-ui

You are in the **chat webview** domain (browser bundle via Vite).

## Allowed
- React components, hooks, CSS, i18n, conversation presentation
- Webview bridge (`src/chat/host/vscodeApi.ts` — this is NOT extension host)
- Message handling that stays on the UI side of `protocol.ts`

## Forbidden without an explicit cross-cutting task
- `src/host/**`, `src/extension.ts`, VS Code `activate` wiring
- Tool executor implementations under `src/tools/**`
- Agent loop / harness runtime under `src/loop/**`, `src/harness/**`
- Adding new Node/`vscode` imports (Vite stubs exist only as a safety net — remove leakage, don't rely on it)

## If host behavior must change
Extend `src/chat/protocol.ts` and implement the handler in `src/host/**` in a **separate, scoped** change — do not pull host modules into the webview.
